nommu-bank: exchange 64 KiB chunks through the ESP32-S3 MMU

Linux RAM is PSRAM behind the cache MMU, mapped in 64 KiB pages. A chunk
of a banked region and its shadow, both aligned, swap two table entries
instead of 128 KiB of PSRAM traffic. The rest still goes word by word.
fork_bank_mmu=0 turns it off; ForkMmuSwapped counts what it moved, and
fork_bank_switch_max=0 clears ForkSwitchMax.

